Finally got the sampler working and it is very fast!

Although there is just one small thing I think I can make better. Right now I am using the following code to calculate a node if it gets updated

        if(model$S[ct]!=prev){
          model$calculate(nodes =dependencies[start_depend[zt]:end_depend[zt]])
          copy(from = model, to = mvSaved, row = 1, nodes = dependencies[start_depend[zt]:end_depend[zt]], logProb = TRUE)
        }

The calculation part works but the copy part gives an error.

Error in eval(accessorVector[[2]], envir = accessorVector[[4]]) :
  object 'zt' not found

There is an easy work around, at the end of the sampler I just do

    copy(from = model, to = mvSaved, row = 1,

         nodes = calcNodes, logProb = TRUE)

Where calcNodes contains all the dependencies. But, because not all nodes change I am copying over values that do not change. I am not sure how inefficient this is, but if you have some suggestions for how to get the first code working I would appreciate it.

Thanks!

