Hi
I have been troubled by this error frequently when trying to fit certain space-time models

samples<-runMCMC(CLSTMCMC,niter=niter,nburnin=3000,nchains=1,thin=1,summary=TRUE,WAIC=TRUE)
running chain 1...
|-------------|-------------|-------------|-------------|
|-------------------------------------------------------|
Error in quantile.default(x, 0.025) :
  missing values and NaN's not allowed if 'na.rm' is FALSE

I don’t have any NAs in the data, but I assume that some thing must produce either NAs or NaNs
in the model run. I would guess it might be some illegal vaue for a sampled parameter but am not sure.

Is there a simple answer for this one?
best
