From uc9e9cbbfb3b043f0 at groups.google.com  Wed Jun  3 14:53:20 2020
From: uc9e9cbbfb3b043f0 at groups.google.com (Daniel Turek)
Date: Wed, 03 Jun 2020 14:53:20 +0000
Subject: Re: A strange error with ST models
Message-ID: <eUdT30mt15k.YlfywE_YAgAJ@nimble-users.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <eUdT30mt15k.3KeMrwrYAgAJ@nimble-users.groups.google.com>
References: <eUdT30mt15k.3KeMrwrYAgAJ@nimble-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/nimble-users/c/eUdT30mt15k/m/YlfywE_YAgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

This is coming up when it tries to calculate the posterior "summary", from your request "summary =  TRUE", which includes the 95% BCIs for all parameters monitored, which uses the R quantile() function.  When quantile() is called on a vector containing one or more NaN values, that's the error you get.  Somewhere in the course of MCMC sampling, a NaN value was generated for at least one of the parameter sample chains.  Without more information about the model, initial values, and the MCMC samplers, it's impossible to diagnose more.  I'd suggest you look at the samples, too, which should also have been returned (samples$samples, I believe), and look at which parameter(s) are giving the NaN samples, and continue to investigate from there.  Bad initial values, or essentially "improper model initialization" is a common source of problems like this.

Keep at it.

Daniel

