Hi Dirk,

Sorry we didn't address your message of a few days ago more quickly.

Are you able to send a minimal reproducible example so we can see the case?

The messages suggest that there was assignment from say a double (numeric) to an integer, which in code-generated C++ may not have behavior you want because types are static.

Superficially your solution makes sense: you are forcing the (NIMBLE) compiler to decide that q is a matrix of doubles, not integers.

But if you have a minimal example, we could look into improving the error-handling of this case.

-Perry

