Hi Chris,

Thank you very much for your response, and I appreciate you taking a look at this. We have been using nimble to fit these types of high-dimensional models to much success. However,  we recently began experiencing these scaling issues, particularly with larger datasets (n>100k).

In our actual application, we have n=2.4 million binary data points and a dense design matrix X that is n x 150. We modified the code using Sally's suggestions. On our high-performance computing system (requested memory of 500gb), it took around 6 hours for the sampler to compile and 95 minutes to generate 2000 samples via the MCMC algorithm. For a n=180k example, it took 16 minutes to compile the sampler and 2 minutes to generate 1k samples via the MCMC algorithm.

Best,
Ben

